{"sections":[],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/spatialtrees"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Trees over points in space that find the points nearest a query, or within a radius or a box."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/KDTree","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/BoundingBox"],"anchor":"k-d-trees","title":"k-d trees"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/Quadtree","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/Octree","doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/SpatialItem"],"anchor":"Quadtrees-and-octrees","title":"Quadtrees and octrees"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/Trees"],"anchor":"Extended-Modules","generated":true,"title":"Extended Modules"}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","title":"SpatialTrees","externalID":"SpatialTrees","role":"collection","symbolKind":"module","modules":[{"name":"SpatialTrees"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/KDTree","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" holds a fixed set of points, SIMD vectors such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SIMD2<Double>"},{"type":"text","text":" or"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SIMD3<Float>"},{"type":"text","text":". It splits them at the median of the first coordinate, then each half at the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"median of the second, cycling through the dimensions, and keeps the result in one flat array"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with no links: every subtree is a contiguous run with its median in the middle."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import SpatialTrees","","let tree = KDTree<SIMD2<Double>>([[2, 3], [5, 4], [9, 6], [4, 7], [8, 1], [7, 2]])","tree.nearestIndex(to: [9, 2])              \/\/ 4: the point [8, 1]","tree.nearestIndices(to: [9, 2], count: 2)  \/\/ [4, 5]","tree.indices(within: 3, of: [5, 5])        \/\/ [1, 3]"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The six points split first on ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"x"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" at the median [7, 2], then each side on ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"y","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":":","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Vertex"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Splits on"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Left subtree"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Right subtree"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"[7, 2]","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"x"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" = 7","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"[5, 4], [2, 3], [4, 7]","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"[9, 6], [8, 1]"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"[5, 4]"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"y"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" = 4","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"[2, 3]"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"[4, 7]","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"[9, 6]"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"y"}]},{"type":"text","text":" = 6"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"[8, 1]"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A search for the point nearest [9, 2] starts on the right of ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"x"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" = 7, finds [8, 1] at distance","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"√2, and skips the whole left side, since the plane ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"x","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" = 7 is 2 away, farther than that. Searches answer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with the indices the points were given at, and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/BoundingBox","type":"reference"},{"text":" describes a box for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/KDTree\/indices(in:)","type":"reference"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The tree’s shape converts to Grafluent’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinaryTree"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinaryTree(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", whose vertices are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the points’ indices."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/Quadtree","type":"reference"},{"text":" and an ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/Octree","type":"reference"},{"text":" hold elements at points, and unlike a k-d tree take insertions","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and removals as the points move. Each splits its region into four (eight) equal cells, and each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"cell again, until every leaf holds at most a bucket of elements; a removal that leaves a cell’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"children holding no more than a bucket merges them back. Searches return ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/SpatialItem","type":"reference"},{"text":" values,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an element with its point.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["var map = Quadtree<String>(bounds: BoundingBox(lower: [0, 0], upper: [100, 100]))","map.insert(\"café\", at: [10, 20])","map.insert(\"station\", at: [80, 75])","map.nearest(to: [11, 19])?.element   \/\/ \"café\"","map.remove(\"café\", at: [10, 20])"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Their cells convert to Grafluent’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RootedTree"},{"text":" with ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RootedTree(_:)"},{"text":", so Grafluent draws the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"subdivision.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"references":{"doc://SpatialTrees/documentation/SpatialTrees/Quadtree":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A quadtree: elements at points in a rectangle, which finds those in a box, within a radius"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of a point, or nearest a point, and takes insertions and removals as the points move."}],"url":"\/documentation\/spatialtrees\/quadtree","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Quadtree","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Quadtree","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"Quadtree","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/Quadtree","role":"symbol"},"doc://SpatialTrees/documentation/SpatialTrees/SpatialItem":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"SpatialItem"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"An item of a quadtree or octree: a point and the element stored at it.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SpatialItem"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/spatialtrees\/spatialitem","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/SpatialItem","title":"SpatialItem","role":"symbol"},"doc://SpatialTrees/documentation/SpatialTrees/Octree":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Octree","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"An octree: elements at points in a box in space, which finds those in a box, within a radius","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of a point, or nearest a point, and takes insertions and removals as the points move.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Octree","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/spatialtrees\/octree","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/Octree","title":"Octree","role":"symbol"},"doc://SpatialTrees/documentation/SpatialTrees":{"url":"\/documentation\/spatialtrees","title":"SpatialTrees","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees","abstract":[{"text":"Trees over points in space that find the points nearest a query, or within a radius or a box.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://SpatialTrees/documentation/SpatialTrees/BoundingBox":{"url":"\/documentation\/spatialtrees\/boundingbox","title":"BoundingBox","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/BoundingBox","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An axis-aligned box: the points whose every coordinate lies between the lower corner’s and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the upper corner’s, both included."}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BoundingBox","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"BoundingBox","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://SpatialTrees/documentation/SpatialTrees/KDTree":{"url":"\/documentation\/spatialtrees\/kdtree","title":"KDTree","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/KDTree","abstract":[{"text":"A k-d tree: a fixed set of points in ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"k","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":" dimensions that finds the points nearest a query, or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"within a radius or a box of it, without testing every point.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"KDTree"}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"KDTree"}]},"doc://SpatialTrees/documentation/SpatialTrees/Trees":{"url":"\/documentation\/spatialtrees\/trees","title":"Trees","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/Trees","abstract":[],"kind":"symbol","role":"collection","type":"topic"},"doc://SpatialTrees/documentation/SpatialTrees/KDTree/indices(in:)":{"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpatialTrees\/documentation\/SpatialTrees\/KDTree\/indices(in:)","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/spatialtrees\/kdtree\/indices(in:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The indices of the points in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"box"},{"type":"text","text":", its faces included, ascending."}],"title":"indices(in:)","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"indices"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"in"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:12SpatialTrees11BoundingBoxV","text":"BoundingBox"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Point"},{"kind":"text","text":">) -> ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":"]"}]}}}